  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Corsican Mastiff Stride** (1 other source): Opened the show; the song comes from the album Getting Into Knives [1]\n- **Soft Targets** (1 other source): Drawn from Bedside Recordings Vol. 1.2, an outlier among the album-based selections [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Choked Out**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **between songs]**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Soft Targets**: back after 29 archived shows (799 days) [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2022-04-30** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 22 songs; 97 min [1]\n- **tmg2022-04-30.aud.mv88.flac24**: audience recording; 21 songs; 98 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: No Children, solo set transition and [1]\n- Taper stood about 12 feet from the stage, on the second level's left side, level with the stage [2]\n- Setlist drew on many albums, including Getting Into Knives, Goths, Heretic Pride, All Hail West Texas, Tallahassee and The Sunset Tree [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2022-04-30**: taped by me; transferred by me; source: SBD > PCM-A10 + CA-14 (healy onstage) > CA-Ugly 2 > PCM-A10 [1]\n- **tmg2022-04-30.aud.mv88.flac24**: taped by One Dozen Cats; source: MV88 > iPhone 8 > WAV (24/48) [2]. Also: Recorded with an MV88 microphone into an iPhone 8, saved as 24-bit/48kHz WAV, edited in REAPER, and converted to FLAC [2]",
